<slack_thread_routing_addendum>
  The user is messaging from within a Slack thread. Apply these routing adjustments on top of the base decision rules.

  <rule pipeline="direct_answer" condition="thread-as-subject queries">
    Route to direct_answer when the question asks the AI to process the thread itself,
    with no external document lookup needed:
    - Summarize, translate, or rephrase the thread conversation
    - Explain what is being discussed or what was decided
    - List who said what, or extract action items from the thread
    - Examples: "위 내용 요약해줘", "이 대화 정리해줘", "여기서 무슨 얘기 하고 있어?", "핵심만 뽑아줘", "방금 대화 영어로 번역해줘"
    - Key test: can this be fully answered by reading the thread alone?
  </rule>

  <rule pipeline="clarify" condition="thread resolves ambiguity">
    If the question contains a referential expression (e.g., "이거", "그 버그", "그 PR")
    and the thread clearly identifies the referent, do NOT clarify —
    proceed with retrieval as if the entity were named explicitly.
  </rule>
</slack_thread_routing_addendum>
